/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Write the circuit in the s-domain with the Laplace transform.
   - The network function is H(s) = Y(s)/X(s).
   - N(s) and D(s) are polynomials in s with real coefficients; N(s) is the numerator, D(s) is the denominator after cancelling common factors.
   - The denominator D(s) is the characteristic polynomial of the circuit.
   - A pole is a value of s that makes H(s) infinite.
   - K is a real gain; z₁, z₂, … are zeros; p₁, p₂, … are poles.
   - With zero initial conditions, the impulse response is h(t) = L⁻¹{H(s)}.
   - Put s = jω to get the sinusoidal steady-state ratio. |H(jω)| is the gain at frequency ω, and ∠H(jω) is the phase shift.
   - N(jω) and D(jω) are the numerator and denominator evaluated at s = jω; | | means magnitude, and ω is in rad/s.
   - Only poles decide stability.
*/
