/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - State variables are the quantities that cannot jump when a switch moves: inductor currents iL and capacitor voltages vC (see initial and final conditions).
   - x is the n × 1 state vector; u holds the m source values; A is n × n and B is n × m.
   - y holds the p chosen outputs; C is p × n.
   - The eigenvalues of A are the natural frequencies of the circuit, the roots of
   - I is the identity matrix of the same size as A.
   - For a series RLC this is the characteristic polynomial s² + (R/L)s + 1/(LC) of second-order RLC circuits, so the eigenvalues show whether the circuit rings without solving any differential equation.
   - Figure 5.9.1 marks the two states on the worked example's circuit.
*/
